WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.200
People don’t know what these&nbsp;
gurus are. Better give them.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.100
Have you made copies or not?

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:13.500
They are making copies in&nbsp;
Sydney now. It is quite a lot

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.600
Horrible!

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.000
It’s a published article on Muktananda.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.400
There’s no, I mean, even the sanctity they have

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.600
that after all, we are talking about God&nbsp;
and what sort of a life we are living.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.600
Worse than a normal person. Much worse.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.200
I don’t know what words there&nbsp;
are in English for such people.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.500
I don’t know even in Hindi language.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:54.600
Horrible! Using thirteen-year-old&nbsp;
girls. Just think of it.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.300
This now has clicked into their heads,&nbsp;
because they are running short of money,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.100
I tell you. In a way it is good, economic problem.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
[Shri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.197
Mataji is laughing]

00:01:36.197 --> 00:01:37.400
We didn’t even ask for this one.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.000
This has come from the advertisement,&nbsp;
you know, the one we put in the paper.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.100
That’s what brought that back. We&nbsp;
didn’t contact them or anything.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.100
For the intensive.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:52.900
Yes.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.800
[Laughter]

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.600
Intensive bhoots.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.893
For intensive removal of your wallet.

00:02:00.893 --> 00:02:06.093
Expensive boots.

00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:10.293
Thank God this much sense has come&nbsp;
that too much glossy advertisement.

00:02:12.793 --> 00:02:13.693
I’ll just go inside.

00:02:13.693 --> 00:02:22.369
It shouldn’t be an intensive, it&nbsp;
should be an expensive, Shri Mataji.

00:02:22.369 --> 00:02:31.193
[Laughter]

00:02:31.193 --> 00:02:37.093
On the contrary, you see, in Sahaja&nbsp;
Yoga, I’ve been so careless about things

00:02:37.093 --> 00:02:42.593
that some leaders have managed to&nbsp;
[unsure: be caught] with money.

00:02:42.593 --> 00:02:46.993
That’s a sad thing, really. It’s a very sad thing.

00:02:49.093 --> 00:02:54.493
I’ve realized it now. Now I’ve&nbsp;
put a clamp on the tour money.

00:02:56.093 --> 00:03:00.293
In this three years’ time, I’ve&nbsp;
been able to achieve such a lot:

00:03:01.393 --> 00:03:07.693
built an ashram in Delhi, we’ve got worship place,

00:03:08.293 --> 00:03:13.793
we’ve got a lot of land in Ganapatipule,&nbsp;
we’ve built in Ganapatipule.

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:17.093
Then also we’ve got land in Pune.

00:03:19.093 --> 00:03:21.793
So many things we’ve done&nbsp;
in this three years’ time!

00:03:24.293 --> 00:03:28.693
And we are, for the last three years,&nbsp;
we are having at least, hundred people

00:03:28.693 --> 00:03:37.793
absolutely free from the third world,&nbsp;
from this, what you call that is?

00:03:37.793 --> 00:03:38.693
[Unclear]

00:03:38.693 --> 00:03:43.993
Yes. All of them are coming&nbsp;
free. Russians, all of them.

00:03:43.993 --> 00:03:47.493
And we have to give them money,&nbsp;
if they don’t even have money

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.893
to take one soft drink for themselves.

00:03:50.893 --> 00:03:53.293
And they have nothing, no money to buy anything.

00:03:53.293 --> 00:03:55.993
We pay them money separately for that.

00:03:58.293 --> 00:04:00.593
At least, four thousand,&nbsp;
five thousand rupees each.

00:04:03.093 --> 00:04:05.394
Then they travel all the way from Delhi.

00:04:07.294 --> 00:04:09.594
And all the traveling also from their own country.

00:04:13.594 --> 00:04:18.694
This time that travel was taken over&nbsp;
by different countries, but still,

00:04:18.694 --> 00:04:20.494
it’s quite a lot of money.

00:04:23.594 --> 00:04:26.294
All these Russians are absolutely free.

00:04:27.094 --> 00:04:29.594
All the Eastern Bloc people are absolutely free.

00:04:32.294 --> 00:04:35.794
Despite that, we have been able to save money.

00:04:35.794 --> 00:04:40.494
What is it?

00:04:40.494 --> 00:04:44.494
And while the prices of everything,&nbsp;
food has gone up in India very much

00:04:44.494 --> 00:04:46.694
in these three years, it has absolutely doubled.

00:04:47.294 --> 00:04:49.594
The prices of silver have gone up, everything.

00:04:51.594 --> 00:04:53.394
That means I don’t know&nbsp;
what these people were doing

00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:56.994
about the money part of it.

00:04:56.994 --> 00:05:00.394
I trusted them, especially from Australia,

00:05:03.694 --> 00:05:04.894
jarring examples.

00:05:17.894 --> 00:05:25.694
I never knew that they would do&nbsp;
money of such a noble work like that.

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:32.194
Now, see, you are here working&nbsp;
and you are collecting money,

00:05:32.194 --> 00:05:33.094
whatever you are doing.

00:05:33.094 --> 00:05:35.494
I mean, if you want to do something wrong,

00:05:35.494 --> 00:05:38.894
I mean, how can I find it out?&nbsp;
It’s possible. It’s not possible.

00:05:39.794 --> 00:05:41.094
How it’s so much possible, Shri Mataji?

00:05:41.994 --> 00:05:44.694
No, I mean, I’ll have to, you&nbsp;
see, as it is I’m so busy.

00:05:46.194 --> 00:05:46.894
How am I to do it?

00:05:47.394 --> 00:05:49.794
In India, it’s very easy&nbsp;
because Babamama is there.

00:05:50.594 --> 00:05:51.794
He’s a chartered accountant.

00:05:51.794 --> 00:05:54.494
He’s not a trustee, so he’s&nbsp;
like a hawk, he sits on that.

00:05:54.494 --> 00:05:56.340
[Laughter]

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.094
He told Me that, “They are so honest”.

00:05:59.094 --> 00:06:02.394
Indians are so honest as far&nbsp;
as God’s money is concerned.

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.094
They never touch it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.896 --> 00:06:12.196
They never touch it. Because they know it has
repercussions.

00:06:13.296 --> 00:06:17.496
He said, “I’ve never seen such&nbsp;
an honest organization as yours”.

00:06:18.596 --> 00:06:19.696
He does everything free.

00:06:19.696 --> 00:06:24.396
Baba does all his accounting, everything free.

00:06:24.396 --> 00:06:27.696
He travels free, does everything&nbsp;
free to all the centres.

00:06:35.096 --> 00:06:38.296
You see, coming here also, he loses a lot of money

00:06:38.296 --> 00:06:40.196
because, you know, he’s a very busy person,

00:06:41.196 --> 00:06:41.796
but he doesn’t mind.

00:06:46.496 --> 00:06:53.196
It’s a situation where one should&nbsp;
understand everybody has to sacrifice,

00:06:53.196 --> 00:06:58.696
not to grab money. One must sacrifice.

00:07:04.096 --> 00:07:06.896
Indians don’t have money, but&nbsp;
they have a sacrificing capacity.

00:07:08.096 --> 00:07:11.696
They’ll have a small little&nbsp;
saving box and in that, every day,

00:07:11.696 --> 00:07:13.196
they go and put it.

00:07:19.496 --> 00:07:23.296
And Indian halls are very expensive,&nbsp;
everything quite expensive there.

00:07:23.296 --> 00:07:30.196
Even to hire these things, very&nbsp;
expensive. And they work it out.

00:07:32.096 --> 00:07:34.696
And even they try to save money in Ganapatipule

00:07:34.696 --> 00:07:36.896
so that you could have a lot of projects.

00:07:36.896 --> 00:07:38.596
I mean, they are really very hard-working people.

00:08:09.496 --> 00:08:13.797
We have also got a very&nbsp;
nice organization now called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.797 --> 00:08:17.097
as ‘Sahaj Women’s
Association’

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:22.547
near Rahuri. I think it’s,&nbsp;
I don’t know how many acres,

00:08:22.547 --> 00:08:33.897
ten or eleven acres of land,&nbsp;
where we have got a kiln

00:08:33.897 --> 00:08:38.147
for making potteries and crockery.

00:08:38.147 --> 00:08:40.297
I mean, lots of things are coming up now.

00:08:41.197 --> 00:08:48.097
And that’s why I bought this crockery&nbsp;
from here, this village craft, Portugal.

00:08:52.897 --> 00:08:59.997
I think they can do it because it’s&nbsp;
very simple, easy things to do.

00:08:59.997 --> 00:09:02.497
We hope the same thing will&nbsp;
happen in Perth, Mother

00:09:02.497 --> 00:09:05.097
with the Giji Ganap thing.

00:09:05.097 --> 00:09:10.197
There’ll be lots of crafts and&nbsp;
arts there. They’ve got the space.

00:09:10.197 --> 00:09:14.197
Once we have our ashram, you see, it’s all right.

00:09:17.397 --> 00:09:18.997
Once we have our ashram, we can do it.

00:09:18.997 --> 00:09:22.797
You all are, and that’s the solution&nbsp;
of this ecological problem also,

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:25.997
arts and crafts.

00:09:27.497 --> 00:09:30.997
That’s why I’m starting this&nbsp;
school also in Ganapatipule,

00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:34.497
what I call the ‘Arts and crafts Society’.

00:09:35.697 --> 00:09:41.297
Twenty-one arts and crafts of India,&nbsp;
where you can go and learn many things.

00:09:49.297 --> 00:09:53.797
We are very good at weaving and&nbsp;
sculpturing and so many things,

00:09:53.797 --> 00:09:58.197
I mean, Indians are really, I&nbsp;
met forty of them, forty artists.

00:09:59.197 --> 00:10:00.397
They are all willing to help.

00:10:03.797 --> 00:10:08.597
In labour, in labour, in&nbsp;
stone. You see that old man?

00:10:09.697 --> 00:10:11.298
We have that, how wonderful he is.

00:10:11.298 --> 00:10:18.198
Mohamed [unclear]. Amazing.

00:10:18.198 --> 00:10:20.598
He’s a Muslim, but he’s got his Realization.

00:10:20.598 --> 00:10:25.098
He’s now dedicated to Sahaja Yoga.&nbsp;
He always stays in that house.

00:10:25.098 --> 00:10:30.198
He does this, does that, all&nbsp;
the time. He’s very good.

00:10:33.498 --> 00:10:39.798
Also, see this, we have got this screen.

00:10:43.598 --> 00:10:47.598
You have so much of wood, and you can create.

00:10:49.798 --> 00:10:55.898
This is from rosewood, but not the,&nbsp;
there are two types of rosewoods we have.

00:10:55.898 --> 00:10:56.998
One we call a ‘shisham’ [Dalbergia sissoo],

00:10:56.998 --> 00:10:57.898
this is from that one.

00:11:03.198 --> 00:11:07.298
But you can make something&nbsp;
that will appeal to you people,

00:11:09.798 --> 00:11:13.598
which will be good for your style.

00:11:15.398 --> 00:11:18.898
But you should know first that&nbsp;
there should be the technique.

00:11:20.498 --> 00:11:23.198
Then creativity comes with Sahaja Yoga.

00:11:24.098 --> 00:11:26.498
Plus, you must adjust it&nbsp;
to the needs of the people.

00:11:29.298 --> 00:11:32.898
Like Gregoire was telling me that our furniture is

00:11:32.898 --> 00:11:39.398
from all sides carved, you see. It’s&nbsp;
humorous. Indians are like that.

00:11:40.198 --> 00:11:43.298
If they are carving a furniture,&nbsp;
the whole thing is carved, you see,

00:11:43.298 --> 00:11:43.898
top to bottom.

00:11:44.998 --> 00:11:47.598
But according to the Western style,&nbsp;
there should be only one line

00:11:47.598 --> 00:11:52.298
and space must be left. There&nbsp;
should be some space in between.

00:11:52.298 --> 00:11:54.998
[Shri Mataji is laughing]

00:11:54.998 --> 00:11:58.898
Like a carpet should not have all&nbsp;
this, just have the line and space.

00:12:00.898 --> 00:12:02.098
All right, you can make it like that.

00:12:09.498 --> 00:12:12.199
Even the wooden things you&nbsp;
make here are so expensive.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:22.700
I bought one bowl for about, I think,&nbsp;
something a hundred and something,

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.900
made of this.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:30.200
I mean, in India, it would&nbsp;
be only five rupees or ten,

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:31.700
ten rupees worth.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:43.400
Because of your labour. This&nbsp;
labour is so nonsensical.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.500
It’s famous all over Australia, labour.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.500
Since long they have achieved this reputation.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.900
And now you are suffering because of them.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:58.700
And why do they need so much money&nbsp;
just to drink? That’s all. Lather.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.900
Australians drink so much,&nbsp;
really. Famous for drinking.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.500
Only Russians can beat them.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.300
Because I’ve gone on international meetings

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:18.700
and I know if an Australian is coming&nbsp;
after drinking to shake your hands,

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.200
be careful. You have to open it like this.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.200
[Laughter]

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.900
And Russians, better put both.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.000
[Laughter]

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.400
So, when are they using that&nbsp;
money also? Nothing for good.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.300
On racehorses.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:35.400
Hum?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:37.900
Drinking and racehorses.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:44.400
Racing horses or going into the&nbsp;
football matches and beating others.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.200
This is… so, it’s nothing so constructive.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:55.600
Nothing productive, you see.&nbsp;
So, all that money is wasted.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:58.500
And then you want more and you want more,

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.600
and this is the situation.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.500
You have so much to eat, everything is there,

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.400
but there are no jobs.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.000
We have the greatest treasure in the world

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.500
to help us on the downward path.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.900
I know, in every way.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.401
But the labour here is to be controlled now.

00:14:20.801 --> 00:14:23.801
I hope they start something&nbsp;
against this drinking, racing.

00:14:25.701 --> 00:14:32.101
And to add to it now are all kinds&nbsp;
of drugs that are pouring in.

00:14:35.601 --> 00:14:36.601
Gurumayi

00:14:36.601 --> 00:14:40.201
And then, now Gurumayi will&nbsp;
starve you. That’s good.

00:14:40.201 --> 00:14:42.401
That’s the only blessing of your economic growth.

00:14:45.001 --> 00:14:51.501
Even in America, now they’ll bundle up.

00:14:51.501 --> 00:14:55.701
They might go now to, I think&nbsp;
now they’ll go to Japan.

00:14:59.001 --> 00:15:00.701
Japan has gone, it’s not good.

00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:04.701
Now, Rajneesh also took his Japanese name ‘Osho’.

00:15:06.701 --> 00:15:09.901
He diverted from one country to&nbsp;
another country to another country,

00:15:09.901 --> 00:15:13.001
you see. Ultimately, he&nbsp;
reached Japan. There he died.

00:15:15.901 --> 00:15:21.601
Now the next move should be&nbsp;
Japanese, Japanese people.

00:15:26.301 --> 00:15:29.901
They don’t drink, Mother, not much anyway.

00:15:31.101 --> 00:15:32.301
But they have money.

00:15:32.301 --> 00:15:33.001
They have a lot of money.

00:15:33.801 --> 00:15:39.701
And quite stupid. They are quite stupid people.

00:15:39.701 --> 00:15:42.301
And they are all right, mechanically&nbsp;
they are all right, you see.

00:15:42.301 --> 00:15:47.201
And they, one person says&nbsp;
anything, everyone follows it.

00:15:47.201 --> 00:15:50.301
That’s one thing with them.&nbsp;
Quite industrious also.

00:15:53.801 --> 00:15:58.701
But they have money and they spend on geishas,

00:15:59.501 --> 00:16:00.301
not on drinking.

00:16:05.701 --> 00:16:12.301
I’ve been to Japan thrice. I&nbsp;
once gave a full bandhan to it.

00:16:12.301 --> 00:16:16.501
Starting right from one end to&nbsp;
another. It just went round.

00:16:16.501 --> 00:16:19.702
I’ve been to places where so&nbsp;
many Japanese have never been.

00:16:40.103 --> 00:16:42.703
But Rajneesh got a lot of&nbsp;
money from Japan and Germany.

00:16:44.903 --> 00:16:47.703
From Japan he got lots of money, lots of money.

00:16:48.403 --> 00:17:04.603
A Rolex diamond watch was a fee.&nbsp;
So that’s how the money is spent.

00:17:06.302 --> 00:17:10.633
Well, they are buying up&nbsp;
Cairns at the rate of knots.

00:17:10.634 --> 00:17:11.145
Buying up?

00:17:11.145 --> 00:17:11.503
Cairns.

00:17:11.503 --> 00:17:12.303
Japanese are.

00:17:12.302 --> 00:17:12.502
Yes.

00:17:16.003 --> 00:17:17.403
They’ll run away because it’s so hot.

00:17:24.103 --> 00:17:26.703
Cairn’s water is also not&nbsp;
good, you get diarrhoea there.

00:17:34.402 --> 00:17:38.502
But it’s like the story of the starfishes,

00:17:38.503 --> 00:17:43.403
how they ran away from Cairns, you see.&nbsp;
All these false gurus have to run away.

00:17:56.402 --> 00:17:57.702
Baba has gone out somewhere?

00:18:12.203 --> 00:18:14.118
He must have gone. He went across to the museum.

00:18:14.118 --> 00:18:14.995
Or having a rest, is it?&nbsp;
Catching upon…He’s upstairs.

00:18:14.995 --> 00:18:15.103
[Hindi]

00:18:15.103 --> 00:18:16.103
So, what is the program?

00:18:17.503 --> 00:18:19.603
There’s nothing now, Shri&nbsp;
Mataji, until this evening.

00:18:20.503 --> 00:18:20.703
Till?

00:18:21.302 --> 00:18:24.503
Till this evening and the public program.

00:18:24.504 --> 00:18:26.804
All right. So, I’ll have some breakfast.

00:18:26.804 --> 00:18:28.884
You can go out for a while, then come back.

00:18:28.884 --> 00:18:29.304
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:18:29.304 --> 00:18:37.204
And my bath. And this puja also&nbsp;
was, I mean, sleeping, sleeping,

00:18:37.204 --> 00:18:40.904
but I had diarrhoea, very bad diarrhoea,&nbsp;
I don’t know. What water you use?

00:18:40.904 --> 00:18:42.404
Please get Evian for Me.

00:18:43.004 --> 00:18:45.704
I think, you see, my stomach is rather sensitive.

00:18:47.304 --> 00:18:52.904
All right? Evian that you get.

00:18:52.904 --> 00:18:53.904
Evian.

00:18:53.904 --> 00:18:57.304
Simple Evian is all right,&nbsp;
not mineral or anything.

00:19:10.404 --> 00:19:12.404
Because I’ve travelled so&nbsp;
much, so it’s better to keep

00:19:12.404 --> 00:19:13.604
to one type of water.

00:19:20.104 --> 00:19:22.754
I’ll take some breakfast, whatever you want.

00:19:22.754 --> 00:19:24.704
Would you like to have it&nbsp;
here now or in your room?

00:19:24.704 --> 00:19:26.904
Hum? I’ll go in the room and have some.

00:19:27.804 --> 00:19:29.704
Today I’ll just eat proteins&nbsp;
and I’ll be all right.

00:19:37.104 --> 00:19:38.104
What water is this one?

00:19:39.004 --> 00:19:39.604
That’s Evian.

00:19:40.204 --> 00:19:40.504
Evian.

00:19:45.304 --> 00:19:49.519
No, it’s not. It’s Vittel.

00:19:49.519 --> 00:19:49.530
Sure?

00:19:49.529 --> 00:19:49.604
It’s something else, Shri Mataji.

00:19:49.604 --> 00:19:53.104
The brand is Vittel. It’s bottled mineral water.

00:19:57.804 --> 00:19:58.804
You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.804 --> 00:19:59.604
don’t get Evian?

00:20:00.404 --> 00:20:01.304
Yes, Shri Mataji.

00:20:01.304 --> 00:20:02.704
Better get it because I don’t know.

00:20:11.204 --> 00:20:13.304
Look at them, how fresh they look!

00:20:16.404 --> 00:20:21.004
Yes, I have [unclear] to the [unclear].

00:20:21.004 --> 00:20:21.408
She must have been surprised at the flowers.

00:20:21.408 --> 00:20:21.704
You have told her from where they come.

00:20:21.704 --> 00:20:34.296
She was very nervous, Shri Mataji.

00:20:34.296 --> 00:20:39.905
But now, I think she was quite deep.&nbsp;
She never asked any stupid questions.

00:20:41.805 --> 00:20:44.005
So young, I was worried this little thing,

00:20:44.005 --> 00:20:53.059
what is she going to do?&nbsp;
You found her out, isn’t it?

00:20:53.059 --> 00:20:53.155
[Shri Mataji is laughing]

00:20:53.155 --> 00:20:58.205
From the local newspaper group, we&nbsp;
were also surprised at the programmes.

00:20:59.305 --> 00:21:00.305
What is the newspaper?

00:21:01.605 --> 00:21:02.905
It’s the Leader Group.

00:21:03.605 --> 00:21:06.105
So, I think she’s from the&nbsp;
local ‘Nun wading’ Gazette.

00:21:08.005 --> 00:21:11.605
So we’ve also advertised to coincide&nbsp;
where we have our public programme,

00:21:12.505 --> 00:21:13.205
around Melbourne.

00:21:14.405 --> 00:21:17.405
It’s nice that the newspaper&nbsp;
themselves are talking against

00:21:17.405 --> 00:21:19.205
the glossy advertisement.

00:21:19.205 --> 00:21:21.905
So, they are concerned. There is a concern.

00:21:22.705 --> 00:21:26.205
But in England, people will&nbsp;
prefer a person who is advertising

00:21:26.205 --> 00:21:30.505
and paying money to the media, you&nbsp;
see. But I think they also realise now.

00:21:32.505 --> 00:21:34.305
They are also running short of money in England.

00:21:35.805 --> 00:21:44.205
America is, that’s a very good place.&nbsp;
That’s one of the advantages of this war.

00:21:49.005 --> 00:21:53.505
Yes, I think that war made a&nbsp;
lot of people stop and think.

00:21:56.505 --> 00:21:59.905
They were quite frightened, Mother,&nbsp;
when it started in Brisbane.

00:21:59.905 --> 00:22:02.605
Other people were crowding&nbsp;
round the television shops,

00:22:02.605 --> 00:22:05.905
and the television shops all had their TVs tuned

00:22:05.905 --> 00:22:11.305
to the cable network news, reporting&nbsp;
the bombing minute by minute.

00:22:11.305 --> 00:22:14.905
And you couldn’t walk past&nbsp;
the crowds of people watching.

00:22:14.905 --> 00:22:19.305
I saw it in the television about this.&nbsp;
So, they were opposing it, is it?

00:22:19.305 --> 00:22:21.405
No, no, they were just so anxious.

00:22:21.405 --> 00:22:23.705
They were worried that this was World War III.

00:22:23.705 --> 00:22:28.506
So, the pavements were full of people&nbsp;
watching every blow-by-blow account.

00:22:30.407 --> 00:22:31.707
They thought it was the end, I think.

00:22:34.307 --> 00:22:41.707
It was the World War III no&nbsp;
doubt, but this war is avoided.

00:22:41.707 --> 00:22:44.507
They were all reading the&nbsp;
prophecies of Nostradamus, Mother.

00:22:47.307 --> 00:22:52.107
Yes, even it is in the Bible, the Jeremiah.

00:22:53.007 --> 00:22:56.507
He’s talked about Babylon. This&nbsp;
is Babylon. Iraq is Babylon.

00:22:56.507 --> 00:22:56.607
Yes.

00:22:57.907 --> 00:22:58.107
It’s there.

00:23:00.307 --> 00:23:03.907
I think this is what he wanted to do,&nbsp;
Shri Mataji, wasn’t it? Saddam Hussein.

00:23:03.907 --> 00:23:07.207
He wanted to recreate the empire of Babylon.

00:23:11.007 --> 00:23:11.507
Yes.

00:23:11.507 --> 00:23:16.507
All he got was a leaning tower&nbsp;
of Babylon. How [unclear].

00:23:19.807 --> 00:23:24.307
In these modern times, he didn’t understand.

00:23:36.107 --> 00:23:40.607
But it’s such a mess now, Mother,&nbsp;
there. The situation is very messy.

00:23:40.607 --> 00:23:42.707
Everybody’s wondering what’s going to happen next.

00:23:43.807 --> 00:23:44.707
About what?

00:23:44.707 --> 00:23:49.107
With the Kurdish refugees&nbsp;
and this whole situation.

00:23:50.807 --> 00:23:53.907
What can Bush do about this? Everybody’s asking.

00:23:58.407 --> 00:24:02.007
Bush is an uncertain quantity. How&nbsp;
can he predict anything about it?

00:24:03.307 --> 00:24:10.607
Very uncertain. Only Miss Thatcher.

00:24:11.607 --> 00:24:15.407
She knew what is to be done about Saddam Hussein.

00:24:16.607 --> 00:24:18.707
That’s the only point where I agreed with her.

00:24:20.107 --> 00:24:21.107
[Laughter]

00:24:21.107 --> 00:24:21.607
Yes, Mother.

00:24:22.707 --> 00:24:26.707
He should be finished. But&nbsp;
otherwise, it’s really too much.

00:24:32.308 --> 00:24:35.608
Otherwise, you know, she is a&nbsp;
very simple woman, otherwise.

00:24:36.708 --> 00:24:40.008
Once what happened, that I was to go to a party,

00:24:40.008 --> 00:24:43.008
to her place, for a lunch, I think.

00:24:43.008 --> 00:24:47.808
And it was, you know, a Monday&nbsp;
or something, and a holiday.

00:24:51.908 --> 00:24:52.508
It was a holiday.

00:24:53.308 --> 00:24:57.908
And all my ornaments were in the bank,&nbsp;
you see. But my daughter had asked Me

00:24:57.908 --> 00:24:59.708
to buy some artificial ornaments.

00:25:01.008 --> 00:25:02.908
So, I said, “Now what to&nbsp;
do? I have nothing to wear.

00:25:03.708 --> 00:25:05.508
C.P. doesn’t like Me to go just like this”.

00:25:05.508 --> 00:25:07.108
So, I said, “All right”.

00:25:07.108 --> 00:25:10.208
So, I wore one of these artificial diamonds.

00:25:10.208 --> 00:25:13.608
Quite big, big ones. Absolutely artificial.

00:25:15.708 --> 00:25:23.208
We went to the lunch. No, it was dinner.&nbsp;
It was a dinner, yes. She saw Me.

00:25:24.408 --> 00:25:28.904
She just started looking at&nbsp;
the diamonds. Her eyes went up.

00:25:28.904 --> 00:25:30.608
[Laughter]

00:25:30.608 --> 00:25:33.208
And she came and talked to Me again and again.

00:25:33.808 --> 00:25:36.508
And then, ultimately, she&nbsp;
asked, “Is it from your family?”

00:25:38.308 --> 00:25:40.908
I did not tell her. I just said, “Yes” or “No”.

00:25:41.808 --> 00:25:43.608
But I was wondering, “Look at this woman.

00:25:45.908 --> 00:25:47.108
She doesn’t even know this”.

00:25:47.108 --> 00:25:49.408
[Shri Mataji is laughing]

00:25:49.408 --> 00:25:52.908
But apart from that, you see,&nbsp;
even if I’m wearing anything,

00:25:52.908 --> 00:25:53.708
what does it matter?

00:25:53.708 --> 00:25:55.408
I’m not going to give it to her in any way.

00:25:57.508 --> 00:25:58.508
[Laughter]

00:25:58.508 --> 00:26:02.908
But the way her eyes, you know,&nbsp;
opened up, I was amazed at her.

00:26:02.908 --> 00:26:04.508
And then she became very friendly with Me.

00:26:04.508 --> 00:26:07.908
She was following Me, neglecting everyone.

00:26:07.908 --> 00:26:11.708
And in the next dinner party&nbsp;
… lunch party, she sat,

00:26:11.708 --> 00:26:13.008
made Me sit with her.

00:26:13.008 --> 00:26:18.508
And she asked lots of things about India,&nbsp;
and “How do you manage your family?”

00:26:18.508 --> 00:26:19.108
and this and that.

00:26:22.808 --> 00:26:25.508
Very surprising, that artificial diamond stuff.

00:26:27.108 --> 00:26:30.108
I told My daughter about it and she just laughed.

00:26:31.608 --> 00:26:35.109
But in England people are quite&nbsp;
conscious of ornaments. Very conscious.

00:26:36.109 --> 00:26:37.309
Maybe here also, I don’t know.

00:26:38.309 --> 00:26:41.409
Not so much. In England they’re&nbsp;
very concerned with status.

00:26:41.409 --> 00:26:41.709
Status.

00:26:42.609 --> 00:26:45.809
Like one day she wore a, I&nbsp;
had an old necklace of mine

00:26:46.409 --> 00:26:47.709
with real pearls, you see.

00:26:47.709 --> 00:26:50.909
They know what real pearls are. I don’t know how.

00:26:50.909 --> 00:26:55.509
And she went to the market. She&nbsp;
went to the shopping and something.

00:26:55.509 --> 00:26:59.009
She came back. She said, “Now&nbsp;
take your madam necklace”.

00:26:59.009 --> 00:27:00.009
I said, “What is this madam?”

00:27:00.709 --> 00:27:03.409
She said, “Mummy, whichever shop&nbsp;
I went, they called Me madam.

00:27:05.309 --> 00:27:07.909
First, I didn’t know what was&nbsp;
how, why have I become madam now.

00:27:09.109 --> 00:27:10.309
Then I realized it was this”.

00:27:11.509 --> 00:27:12.509
[Laughter]

00:27:12.509 --> 00:27:17.609
Once I was, I have lots of such&nbsp;
things with Me because of the family.

00:27:17.609 --> 00:27:23.309
So, I was wearing one ring with a big emerald.

00:27:23.309 --> 00:27:26.909
Very big emerald it is. Such a&nbsp;
big one. It’s from the family.

00:27:26.909 --> 00:27:29.009
I don’t know, I mean, in&nbsp;
India nobody would look at you

00:27:29.009 --> 00:27:31.109
for that. So…

00:27:31.109 --> 00:27:31.976
[Cut in the audio]

00:27:31.976 --> 00:27:36.909
…Well, everybody has to bow to her. But&nbsp;
she’s a sweet lady. She didn’t mind.

00:27:39.109 --> 00:27:42.909
There’s a story, Mother,&nbsp;
of King Charles the first,

00:27:42.909 --> 00:27:48.509
and he was riding through Scotland&nbsp;
and he came across a man belonging to

00:27:48.509 --> 00:27:51.209
some very small Christian&nbsp;
group who didn’t approve.

00:27:52.609 --> 00:27:56.909
And his lieutenants, they were all on horses

00:27:56.909 --> 00:27:59.009
and this man was on foot and his lieutenants said,

00:27:59.709 --> 00:28:02.109
“Will you not take your hat&nbsp;
off before the king, sir?”

00:28:03.109 --> 00:28:05.309
And the Scotsman, who was very independent, said,

00:28:06.009 --> 00:28:07.309
“No, Jimmy, I won’t!”

00:28:07.909 --> 00:28:11.309
And so, the king said, “Then, sir,&nbsp;
I will take my hat off to you”.

00:28:11.309 --> 00:28:12.980
And he took it off.

00:28:12.981 --> 00:28:15.910
[Laughter]

00:28:15.909 --> 00:28:22.009
He was a gracious man, apparently.&nbsp;
Perhaps it was King Charles II.

00:28:22.809 --> 00:28:26.209
He must have been the same man who&nbsp;
was going up the stairs, wasn’t he?

00:28:26.909 --> 00:28:27.509
Yes, he was.

00:28:28.909 --> 00:28:31.709
But you see, it’s all right.

00:28:31.709 --> 00:28:35.510
I mean, supposing it’s your&nbsp;
country, it’s all right.

00:28:36.611 --> 00:28:40.311
But we are from another country. We&nbsp;
are not even in the Commonwealth.

00:28:42.311 --> 00:28:49.501
So, may I make everyone bow to her?&nbsp;
The Chilean-Americans should say, “Hi!”

00:28:49.501 --> 00:28:49.511
[Laughter]

00:28:49.511 --> 00:29:02.601
I think some of them do.

00:29:02.601 --> 00:29:02.611
[Laughter]

00:29:02.611 --> 00:29:04.311
Rosy, are you going to America now?

00:29:04.311 --> 00:29:05.211
Yes, Mother.

00:29:05.211 --> 00:29:05.511
When?

00:29:09.211 --> 00:29:10.411
I’m not sure when.

00:29:14.711 --> 00:29:25.111
How is she? Thank you. Are you&nbsp;
all right? So grown up… Oh, my.

00:29:25.111 --> 00:29:31.811
[Cut in the audio]

00:29:31.811 --> 00:29:34.211
I live in one week and then&nbsp;
a few weeks after that.

00:29:35.111 --> 00:29:37.611
Somewhere between one month and three months.

00:29:37.611 --> 00:29:39.411
I see. So where will you be?

00:29:39.411 --> 00:29:46.811
Seattle. If that’s OK.

00:29:46.811 --> 00:29:47.211
Very good.

00:30:03.611 --> 00:30:04.711
And when do you love Me?

00:30:06.411 --> 00:30:07.411
[Laughter]

00:30:07.411 --> 00:30:08.311
All the time.

00:30:09.111 --> 00:30:14.261
Very sweet. She’s a poetess. So sweet.

00:30:14.261 --> 00:30:28.811
Ganesha is standing in attention for&nbsp;
you, really. It’s beautiful. Thank you.

00:30:28.811 --> 00:30:32.511
You ask them to keep it carefully&nbsp;
somewhere. They will do it.

00:30:33.111 --> 00:30:38.212
There. Give it to Kay. I’m very happy now.

00:30:39.412 --> 00:30:40.712
So, you are enjoying yourself?

00:30:41.512 --> 00:30:43.312
Very much, Shri Mataji. Very, very much.

00:30:44.512 --> 00:30:45.812
Rosy looks so nice.

00:30:56.812 --> 00:31:01.612
That Philip is such a stupid fool. He’s&nbsp;
doing all kinds of things in France.

00:31:02.412 --> 00:31:07.112
He’s going on the streets and shouting,&nbsp;
I am the incarnation and this and that.

00:31:08.312 --> 00:31:12.512
Big problems. I said, “Let him shout.&nbsp;
He’ll go into a lunatic asylum”.

00:31:13.912 --> 00:31:15.312
Lots of lunatics are there.

00:31:15.912 --> 00:31:16.612
There are.

00:31:16.612 --> 00:31:17.512
They are on the streets.

00:31:18.312 --> 00:31:18.912
I’ve seen them.

00:31:21.012 --> 00:31:23.112
They are not in the lunatic&nbsp;
asylum but on the street,

00:31:23.112 --> 00:31:25.112
and they go with you in the buses

00:31:25.112 --> 00:31:28.412
and things and talking all kinds&nbsp;
of things, you know, horrible.

00:31:31.012 --> 00:31:35.412
And I told Marie, “What is this nonsense?&nbsp;
They put all of them on the streets

00:31:35.412 --> 00:31:37.112
and they are walking into every bus.

00:31:38.112 --> 00:31:42.812
So she told Me that, “Mother, you&nbsp;
see, we French are very considerate

00:31:43.512 --> 00:31:44.812
and we try to help them”.

00:31:44.812 --> 00:31:48.812
I said, “What? You are helping&nbsp;
them and ruining everybody else.

00:31:48.812 --> 00:31:53.912
This is not, this is a stupid type&nbsp;
of help that you are giving them.

00:31:53.912 --> 00:31:55.912
Better put them in some lunatic asylum”.

00:32:03.512 --> 00:32:05.312
French are coming up now, they look better.

00:32:07.212 --> 00:32:09.012
They seem much happier.

00:32:09.012 --> 00:32:13.512
When I saw the people that I knew there,&nbsp;
they seemed very joyful and really…

00:32:13.512 --> 00:32:14.212
Better now.

00:32:14.212 --> 00:32:16.312
Very good, very good.

00:32:16.312 --> 00:32:18.112
Very much changed, yes.

00:32:19.212 --> 00:32:21.512
You see, in that country, if you are miserable,

00:32:21.512 --> 00:32:22.712
then you are very knowledgeable.

00:32:24.412 --> 00:32:29.612
You have to live very miserable,&nbsp;
extremely unhappy all the time.

00:32:31.912 --> 00:32:35.112
If you are not miserable,&nbsp;
then you are an ignoramus.

00:32:36.712 --> 00:32:38.912
Can you imagine? ‘Les Misérables’.

00:32:44.313 --> 00:32:45.313
[Laughter]

00:32:45.313 --> 00:32:53.013
She’s still downward [unsure].&nbsp;
She’s happy to go to America?

00:32:53.613 --> 00:32:54.613
Yes, Mother.

00:32:54.613 --> 00:32:57.413
Better send her Baba to school,&nbsp;
that America is horrible.

00:32:59.113 --> 00:32:59.813
She can go, but…

00:33:01.613 --> 00:33:03.213
What has happened to Gregoire’s children,

00:33:03.213 --> 00:33:04.413
I’m really frightened now.

00:33:07.213 --> 00:33:09.613
When he took them down to New&nbsp;
York, I mean, they are living

00:33:09.613 --> 00:33:10.813
in a very posh locality,

00:33:13.113 --> 00:33:20.213
the children from the neighbourhood&nbsp;
started beating these children.

00:33:20.213 --> 00:33:23.813
Then they brought some sort of hammers&nbsp;
and things to beat these children.

00:33:24.713 --> 00:33:26.013
So, they came up to their father.

00:33:26.713 --> 00:33:30.913
Father went and saw the parents&nbsp;
and they said, “You must control

00:33:30.913 --> 00:33:33.913
your children the way they&nbsp;
are, very violent type”.

00:33:33.913 --> 00:33:36.313
They said, “They were just like&nbsp;
your children to begin with.

00:33:37.913 --> 00:33:40.413
But we found out, if they have to live here,

00:33:40.413 --> 00:33:42.413
they have to be like this.&nbsp;
So, we have allowed them.

00:33:43.213 --> 00:33:44.913
You have to allow your children to be the same”.

00:33:46.513 --> 00:33:48.513
So Gregoire immediately packed them off to India.

00:33:51.513 --> 00:33:59.213
You like to go to India? Ah, see!&nbsp;
I think there’s not a way out.

00:34:05.013 --> 00:34:09.313
You can take her down there, it’s&nbsp;
all right, but it’s horrible…

00:34:09.313 --> 00:34:11.913
Mother, we were going to&nbsp;
take her for a little while,

00:34:11.913 --> 00:34:13.413
and then send her to India.

00:34:13.413 --> 00:34:15.213
That’s what I said, you take&nbsp;
her there for a little while.

00:34:16.213 --> 00:34:17.613
And then you send her over.

00:34:17.614 --> 00:34:22.414
Just so she is established in our&nbsp;
families, a bit more established.

00:34:23.913 --> 00:34:26.913
Yes. As it is, she has had&nbsp;
a very hard time actually.

00:34:33.114 --> 00:34:36.614
It’s schizophrenia, you see,&nbsp;
that goes and comes back,

00:34:36.614 --> 00:34:38.114
goes and comes back.

00:34:38.114 --> 00:34:42.715
But only the frequency is so big now,&nbsp;
that you don’t know whether it’s cured

00:34:42.715 --> 00:34:46.615
or not, somebody is cured&nbsp;
or not. It comes and goes.

00:34:54.915 --> 00:34:55.515
Just can’t see.

00:35:00.715 --> 00:35:05.015
Also, one should work it out,&nbsp;
you see, then it might go away.

00:35:05.015 --> 00:35:10.915
But if somebody is not coordinating&nbsp;
or cooperating, then it’s impossible.

00:35:14.315 --> 00:35:15.115
It just settles.

00:35:33.515 --> 00:35:34.515
All right, so, should we?

00:35:35.015 --> 00:35:43.112
I’ll have my breakfast, and then we can go out

00:35:43.112 --> 00:35:55.315
for [unclear], you see.

00:35:55.315 --> 00:35:58.215
This little girl also found it&nbsp;
difficult to get out of these seats.

00:36:01.115 --> 00:36:03.415
I think we should have little higher seats.

00:36:03.415 --> 00:36:05.015
That’s why you people all give in here.

00:36:06.515 --> 00:36:10.515
Little higher seats, would be better&nbsp;
so that to get up would be easier.

00:36:10.515 --> 00:36:29.606
[Hindi conversation]

00:36:29.606 --> 00:36:42.015
Shri Mataji?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:42.015 --> 00:36:44.716
Last time you came there were two Chilean people

00:36:44.716 --> 00:36:47.816
came to your program. It’s&nbsp;
now grown to over twelve.

00:36:48.416 --> 00:36:53.816
We have programs very regularly, once&nbsp;
a week, out on the eastern suburbs.

00:36:53.816 --> 00:36:55.016
This is the main family.

00:36:57.016 --> 00:36:59.375
There were five or six South&nbsp;
American people last night.

00:36:59.375 --> 00:36:59.382
Really?

00:36:59.382 --> 00:36:59.386
Yes?

00:36:59.386 --> 00:36:59.407
Yes, I saw this lady.

00:36:59.407 --> 00:37:06.616
She came at your puja last&nbsp;
night, and she was so excited,

00:37:06.616 --> 00:37:11.516
you couldn’t believe it. And&nbsp;
this lady too. They’re so strong.

00:37:12.916 --> 00:37:16.816
They just say that, “We give a bandhan,&nbsp;
ask Mother, and everything happens.

00:37:16.816 --> 00:37:20.316
It’s just quite extraordinary”.&nbsp;
They’re teaching us Sahaja Yoga.

00:37:20.316 --> 00:37:24.116
This lady had lost her daughter&nbsp;
here. This girl had run away.

00:37:24.116 --> 00:37:26.016
And she’d been coming for two weeks.

00:37:26.016 --> 00:37:28.816
She sat before your photograph&nbsp;
and she said, “Mother,

00:37:28.816 --> 00:37:31.016
I don’t know what to do. I&nbsp;
don’t know how to handle it.

00:37:31.016 --> 00:37:32.716
You take care of it for me”.

00:37:32.716 --> 00:37:36.916
And she said, “Every hair on her&nbsp;
body stood on end. Every hair”.

00:37:37.616 --> 00:37:39.516
And she said, “Then I knew it would be all right”.

00:37:39.516 --> 00:37:40.716
One week, the daughter came back.

00:37:40.716 --> 00:37:49.616
The same lady. Her experiences are amazing.

00:37:49.616 --> 00:37:50.616
This is another lady.

00:37:51.216 --> 00:37:53.516
Her husband comes more,&nbsp;
but she’s coming sometimes.

00:37:53.516 --> 00:37:54.436
[Unclear] little boy.

00:37:54.436 --> 00:37:57.064
Yes, Chileans are very good.&nbsp;
And I’m going to go to Chile.

00:37:57.064 --> 00:37:58.465
Mother, they’ll be so pleased.

00:37:58.465 --> 00:38:04.598
I will go to Chile. But that&nbsp;
will be later. Let’s decide it.

00:38:04.598 --> 00:38:10.816
You have to ask them when the climate is good.

00:38:12.416 --> 00:38:16.516
This lady gave Realization to her&nbsp;
brother on the phone in Chile.

00:38:17.516 --> 00:38:17.816
Really?

00:38:18.916 --> 00:38:19.116
Yes.

00:38:19.116 --> 00:38:19.449
She’s very powerful.

00:38:19.449 --> 00:38:22.316
And she said at nine o’clock&nbsp;
in the evening she would give

00:38:22.316 --> 00:38:24.216
a bandhan to him.

00:38:24.216 --> 00:38:26.416
And he rang up and said, “What’s&nbsp;
happening at nine o’clock

00:38:26.416 --> 00:38:28.516
in the morning?” Because&nbsp;
it’s twelve hours difference.

00:38:28.516 --> 00:38:31.916
“I was so peaceful. So peaceful.&nbsp;
I don’t know what’s happening”.

00:38:33.416 --> 00:38:34.168
She’s very powerful.

00:38:34.168 --> 00:38:34.616
Yes, she’s lovely.

00:38:36.616 --> 00:38:37.907
That’s her heart.

00:38:37.907 --> 00:38:39.116
Yes, the heart is just so huge.

00:38:39.116 --> 00:38:42.816
She’s a great seeker too.

00:38:42.816 --> 00:38:45.116
They’ll all be at your&nbsp;
program tonight and tomorrow.

00:38:47.616 --> 00:38:52.067
So, we have to contact you,&nbsp;
I think, when I go there.

00:38:52.067 --> 00:38:52.917
All right, they’ll be so happy.

00:38:53.717 --> 00:38:55.617
They heard last year that you were going to go

00:38:55.617 --> 00:38:57.317
and it was cancelled. But…

00:38:57.317 --> 00:39:01.817
Yes. I don’t know what time we should go there.

00:39:01.817 --> 00:39:04.117
Just try to adjust to come out.

00:39:04.117 --> 00:39:06.317
I’ll speak to them. I’ll speak to them tonight.

00:39:06.317 --> 00:39:10.117
Just ask what is the best time. You said August.

00:39:10.917 --> 00:39:12.817
Yes, I’m not sure. I’ll have to ask them.

00:39:12.817 --> 00:39:14.617
August is better.

00:39:14.617 --> 00:39:17.317
Some of them are already talking&nbsp;
about and they’re really…

00:39:17.317 --> 00:39:21.217
[Cut in the audio]

00:39:21.217 --> 00:39:24.117
Some have only been here for&nbsp;
maybe three or four months

00:39:24.117 --> 00:39:26.117
and they’re starting to have that vision already

00:39:26.117 --> 00:39:29.817
that when they’ve grown a little&nbsp;
bit then they go back to Chile

00:39:29.817 --> 00:39:31.044
and work for Sahaja Yoga.

00:39:31.044 --> 00:39:33.449
All right. You come here.&nbsp;
I have to talk to you also.

00:39:33.450 --> 00:39:34.267
[End of recording]

